{"name":"Flagstone","hex":"#acadad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flagstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat, rectangular piece of rock or stone used for paving or roofing.","One of several types of rock easily split and suitable for making flagstones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flagstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flagstone","blocks":[{"text":"A flagstone, or flag, is a generic flat stone, sometimes cut in regular rectangular or square shape and usually used for paving slabs or walkways, patios, flooring, fences and roofing. It may be used for memorials, headstones, facades and other construction. The name derives from Middle English flagge meaning turf, perhaps from Old Norse flaga meaning 'slab' or 'chip'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Portage_Park_Chicago_flagstone_steps.JPG/330px-Portage_Park_Chicago_flagstone_steps.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flagstone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Westray_House.jpg/500px-Westray_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Westray_House.jpg/500px-Westray_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"House on Westray, Orkney, with flagstone roof","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWestray_House.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Cloister_of_the_University_of_Bergamo._Italy.jpg/500px-Cloister_of_the_University_of_Bergamo._Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Cloister_of_the_University_of_Bergamo._Italy.jpg/1280px-Cloister_of_the_University_of_Bergamo._Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig